{"abstract":"Millions of consumers search for products online each day, aiming to find items that meet their needs at an acceptable price. While price and quality are major factors in purchasing decisions, ethical considerations increasingly influence consumer behavior—giving rise to the socially responsible consumer. Insights from a recent survey of over 600 consumers reveal that many barriers to ethical shopping stem from information-seeking challenges, often leading to decisions made under uncertainty. These challenges contribute to the intention–behaviour gap, where consumers’ desire to make ethical choices is undermined by limited or inaccessible information and inefficacy of search systems in supporting responsible decision-making. In this perspectives paper, we argue that the field of Information Retrieval (IR) has a critical role to play by empowering consumers to make more informed and more responsible choices. We present three interrelated perspectives: (1) reframing responsible consumption as an information extraction problem aimed at reducing information asymmetries; (2) redefining product search as a complex task requiring interfaces that lower the cost and burden of responsible search; and (3) reimagining search as a process of knowledge calibration that helps consumers bridge gaps in awareness when making purchasing decisions. Taken together, these perspectives outline a path from query to conscience — one where IR systems help transform everyday product searches into opportunities for more ethical and informed choices. We advocate for the development of new and novel IR systems and interfaces that address the intricacies of socially responsible consumerism, and call on the IR community to build technologies that make ethical decisions more informed, convenient, and aligned with economic realities.","author_count":3,"contributors":["van der Sluis, Frans","Azzopardi, Leif","Meier, Florian Maximilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805140"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Glasgow"],"keyword":["Ethical Consumerism","Online shopping"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"from query to conscience the importance of information retrieval in empowering socially responsible consumerism","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3726302.3730347","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 Research and Innovation program under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 860721 (DoSSIER)."],"id":"S01-000.00-805140","identifier":[{"id":"105011829046","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-77308b4b-ce8f-4fcb-8582-dadc664125b0"],"keyword":["Ethical Consumerism","Online Shopping","Socially Responsible Shopping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E111D93948CA35C9A9581F70931CB85F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3726302.3730347","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/778510628/0_sigir2025_short.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of glasgow","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Glasgow","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frans","key":"vandersluispau","last":"van der Sluis","name":"van der Sluis, Frans","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leif","key":"azzopardipau","last":"Azzopardi","name":"Azzopardi, Leif","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3726302.3730347","eisbn":["9798400715921"],"pages":"3853-3864","status":"p","title":"SIGIR 2025 - Proceedings of the 48th International ACM SIGIR Conference on Research and Development in Information Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105011829046"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-77308b4b-ce8f-4fcb-8582-dadc664125b0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"From Query to Conscience: The Importance of Information Retrieval in Empowering Socially Responsible Consumerism","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805140","year":"2025",