, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of regensburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Regensburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"elsweilerpau","last":"Elsweiler","name":"Elsweiler, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0f9e908e-58bb-4fde-9aa5-5f0beb884a83"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Empirically measuring algorithmically embodied emissions of information access systems","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-814221","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Cells change their metabolic profiles in response to underlying gene regulatory networks, but how can alterations in metabolism encode specific transcriptional instructions? Here, we show that forcing a metabolic change in embryonic stem cells (ESCs) promotes a developmental identity that better approximates the inner cell mass (ICM) of the early mammalian blastocyst in cultures. This shift in cellular identity depends on the inhibition of glycolysis and stimulation of oxidative phosphorylation (OXPHOS) triggered by the replacement of d-glucose by d-galactose in ESC media. Enhanced OXPHOS in turn activates NAD + -dependent deacetylases of the Sirtuin family, resulting in the deacetylation of histones and key transcription factors to focus enhancer activity while reducing transcriptional noise, which results in a robustly enhanced ESC phenotype. This exploitation of a NAD + /NADH coenzyme coupled to OXPHOS as a means of programming lineage-specific transcription suggests new paradigms for how cells respond to alterations in their environment, and implies cellular rejuvenation exploits enzymatic activities for simultaneous activation of a discrete enhancer set alongside silencing genome-wide transcriptional noise.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Bone, Robert A","Lowndes, Molly","Raineri, Silvia","Redó-Riveiro, Alba","Lundregan, Sarah L.","Dall, Morten","Sulek, Karolina","Romero Herrera, Jose Alejandro","Malzard, Luna","Koigi, Sandra","Heckenbach, Indra","Solis-Mezarino, Victor","Völker-Albert, Moritz","Vasilopoulou, Catherine G.","Meier, Florian","Trusina, Ala","Mann, Matthias","Nielsen, Michael L.","Treebak, Jonas T.","Brickman, Joshua M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819389"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","Moleqlar Analytics GmbH"],"keyword":["Aging","Enhancers","Metabolism","Pluripotency","Sirtuins"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"altering metabolism programs cell identity via nad sup sup dependent deacetylation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44318-025-00417-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819389","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12130289","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40281356","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003470286","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-74dec761-95cb-4fa2-b341-b1b088833615"],"keyword":["Aging","Enhancers","Metabolism","Pluripotency","Sirtuins"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2BFB5E91F18479A0B75AC066B5DBF0E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/449126031/bone-et-al-altering-metabolism-programs-cell-identity-via-nad-dependent-deacetylation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44318-025-00417-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Dept. of Biomedical Sciences, reNEW, Brickman Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"moleqlar analytics gmbh","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Moleqlar Analytics GmbH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Robert A.","key":"bonepau","last":"Bone","locid":"fd8ee879-f772-406e-958e-a9930ed30523","name":"Bone, Robert A","name_org":"Bone, Robert A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Molly P.","key":"lowndespau","last":"Lowndes","locid":"a9273238-2183-49d8-805d-9cc0aac7fcd9","name":"Lowndes, Molly","name_org":"Lowndes, Molly P.","orcid":"0000-0003-3692-7847","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Silvia","key":"raineripau","last":"Raineri","locid":"090b8f75-25c0-42d0-8d10-e51aef33cf85","name":"Raineri, Silvia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alba","key":"rriveiropau","last":"R Riveiro","locid":"6ee68a94-132a-4737-abea-dbf13dbe6de7","name":"Redó-Riveiro, Alba","name_org":"R Riveiro, Alba","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah L.","key":"lundreganpau","last":"Lundregan","locid":"0431ad25-511f-4426-9df7-bbedfd58e98c","name":"Lundregan, Sarah L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"dallpau","last":"Dall","locid":"16f23ce0-9a8b-4fb9-ad56-835399aae31d","name":"Dall, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-8577-3162","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karolina","key":"sulekpau","last":"Sulek","locid":"dfe091b3-bc3a-40cb-b540-ce37005de114","name":"Sulek, Karolina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jose A.H.","key":"romeropau","last":"Romero","locid":"529a677f-f0cf-49ce-8367-9ffa8acda16e","name":"Romero Herrera, Jose Alejandro","name_org":"Romero, Jose A.H.","orcid":"0000-0002-4765-2087","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Luna","key":"malzardpau","last":"Malzard","name":"Malzard, Luna","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sandra","key":"koigipau","last":"Koigi","name":"Koigi, Sandra","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Indra J.","key":"heckenbachpau","last":"Heckenbach","locid":"b02b1552-5fc6-4f4e-9b39-0c501811f812","name":"Heckenbach, Indra","name_org":"Heckenbach, Indra J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Victor","key":"solismezarinopau","last":"Solis-Mezarino","name":"Solis-Mezarino, Victor","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Moritz","key":"völkeralbertpau","last":"Völker-Albert","name":"Völker-Albert, Moritz","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Catherine G.","key":"vasilopouloupau","last":"Vasilopoulou","name":"Vasilopoulou, Catherine G.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ala","key":"trusinapau","last":"Trusina","locid":"94af13f2-dd1e-4c9b-a531-3cf33052ef9f","name":"Trusina, Ala","orcid":"0000-0003-1945-454X","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"lnielsenpau","last":"L Nielsen","locid":"b72d98f7-79fa-43a7-8066-783ed8034146","name":"Nielsen, Michael L.","name_org":"L Nielsen, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-0067-9039","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas T.","key":"treebakpau","last":"Treebak","locid":"a648ef82-ccb3-4add-83c1-384e0d90952b","name":"Treebak, Jonas T.","orcid":"0000-0003-1488-7012","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Joshua M.","key":"brickmanpau","last":"Brickman","locid":"7eb57bef-9866-4e13-981e-34c12c3ad759","name":"Brickman, Joshua M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1580-7491","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40281356"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s44318-025-00417-0","issn":["02614189","14602075"],"issn_org":["02614189"],"issue":"11","journal":"EMBO Journal","pages":"3056-3084","status":"p","title":"EMBO Journal","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105003470286"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-74dec761-95cb-4fa2-b341-b1b088833615"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Altering metabolism programs cell identity via NAD<sup>+</sup>-dependent deacetylation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819389","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Optimizing data-independent acquisition (DIA) methods for proteomics applications often requires balancing spectral resolution and acquisition speed. Here we describe a real-time, full mass range implementation of the Phase-constrained Spectrum Deconvolution Method (ΦSDM) for Orbitrap TM mass spectrometry that increases mass resolving power without increasing scan time. Comparing its performance to the standard enhanced Fourier transformation (eFT) signal processing revealed that the increased resolving power of ΦSDM is beneficial in areas of high peptide density and comes with a greater ability to resolve low-abundance signals. In a standard 2-hour analysis of a 200 ng HeLa digest, this resulted in an increase of 16% in the number of quantified peptides. As the acquisition speed becomes even more important when using fast chromatographic gradients, we further applied ΦSDM methods to a range of shorter gradient lengths (21, 12, and 5 min). While ΦSDM improved identification rates and spectral quality in all tested gradients, it proved particularly advantageous for the 5 min gradient. Here the number of identified protein groups and peptides increased by >15% in comparison to eFT processing. In conclusion, ΦSDM is an alternative signal processing algorithm for processing Orbitrap data that can improve spectral quality and benefit quantitative accuracy in typical proteomics experiments, especially when using short gradients.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Steigerwald, Sophia","Sinha, Ankit","Fort, Kyle L","Zeng, Wen-Feng","Niu, Lili","Wichmann, Christoph","Kreutzmann, Arne","Mourad, Daniel","Aizikov, Konstantin","Grinfeld, Dmitry","Makarov, Alexander","Mann, Matthias","Meier, Florian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-720403"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Jena University Hospital","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Thermo Fisher Scientific (Bremen) GmbH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"full mass range φsdm orbitrap mass spectrometry for dia proteome analysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2024.100713","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-720403","identifier":[{"id":"85184859404","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10851225","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38184013","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5d601648-e25e-4e15-b3b3-364e68024d68"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F030B8DE89B8A79FD32356F423668CDD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2024.100713","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381796804/1_s2.0_S1535947624000033_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Thermo Fisher Scientific (Bremen) GmbH"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Mann Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"jena university hospital","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Jena University Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sophia","key":"steigerwaldpau","last":"Steigerwald","name":"Steigerwald, Sophia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ankit","key":"sinhapau","last":"Sinha","name":"Sinha, Ankit","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kyle L","key":"fortpau","last":"Fort","name":"Fort, Kyle L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wen-Feng","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Wen-Feng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lili","key":"niupau","last":"Niu","locid":"f74df5eb-9404-4bdb-9d58-289bf2c90efa","name":"Niu, Lili","orcid":"0000-0003-4571-4368","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoph","key":"wichmannpau","last":"Wichmann","name":"Wichmann, Christoph","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Arne","key":"kreutzmannpau","last":"Kreutzmann","name":"Kreutzmann, Arne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Daniel","key":"mouradpau","last":"Mourad","name":"Mourad, Daniel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Konstantin","key":"aizikovpau","last":"Aizikov","name":"Aizikov, Konstantin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Dmitry","key":"grinfeldpau","last":"Grinfeld","name":"Grinfeld, Dmitry","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alexander","key":"makarovpau","last":"Makarov","name":"Makarov, Alexander","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38184013"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcpro.2024.100713","issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","paperid":"100713","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184859404"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5d601648-e25e-4e15-b3b3-364e68024d68"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Full Mass Range ΦSDM Orbitrap Mass Spectrometry for DIA Proteome Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-720403","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In common with other omics technologies, mass spectrometry (MS)-based proteomics produces ever-increasing amounts of raw data, making efficient analysis a principal challenge. A plethora of different computational tools can process the MS data to derive peptide and protein identification and quantification. However, during the last years there has been dramatic progress in computer science, including collaboration tools that have transformed research and industry. To leverage these advances, we develop AlphaPept, a Python-based open-source framework for efficient processing of large high-resolution MS data sets. Numba for just-in-time compilation on CPU and GPU achieves hundred-fold speed improvements. AlphaPept uses the Python scientific stack of highly optimized packages, reducing the code base to domain-specific tasks while accessing the latest advances. We provide an easy on-ramp for community contributions through the concept of literate programming, implemented in Jupyter Notebooks. Large datasets can rapidly be processed as shown by the analysis of hundreds of proteomes in minutes per file, many-fold faster than acquisition. AlphaPept can be used to build automated processing pipelines with web-serving functionality and compatibility with downstream analysis tools. It provides easy access via one-click installation, a modular Python library for advanced users, and via an open GitHub repository for developers.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Strauss, Maximilian T.","Bludau, Isabell","Zeng, Wen-Feng","Voytik, Eugenia","Ammar, Constantin","Schessner, Julia P.","Ilango, Rajesh","Gill, Michelle","Meier, Florian","Willems, Sander","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747666"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["Mass Spectrometry methods","Proteome","Proteomics methods","Software"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Nvidia Corporation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"alphapept a modern and open framework for ms based proteomics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-46485-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747666","identifier":[{"id":"38461149","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85187135226","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10924963","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-26cd1ce9-9929-4b9e-89ed-39aacb727cd3"],"keyword":["Mass Spectrometry/methods","Proteome","Proteomics/methods","Software"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0712762AFF761093FE6409733F33CB33"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/400216148/s41467_024_46485_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-46485-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Mann Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Nvidia Corporation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maximilian T.","key":"strausspau","last":"Strauss","locid":"c396d94e-014c-4f75-9272-f7795bbc8b4f","name":"Strauss, Maximilian T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Isabell","key":"bludaupau","last":"Bludau","name":"Bludau, Isabell","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Wen-Feng","key":"zengpau","last":"Zeng","name":"Zeng, Wen-Feng","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eugenia","key":"voytikpau","last":"Voytik","name":"Voytik, Eugenia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Constantin","key":"ammarpau","last":"Ammar","name":"Ammar, Constantin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julia P.","key":"schessnerpau","last":"Schessner","name":"Schessner, Julia P.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Rajesh","key":"ilangopau","last":"Ilango","name":"Ilango, Rajesh","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michelle","key":"gillpau","last":"Gill","name":"Gill, Michelle","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sander","key":"willemspau","last":"Willems","name":"Willems, Sander","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38461149"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-46485-4","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"2168","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85187135226"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-26cd1ce9-9929-4b9e-89ed-39aacb727cd3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"AlphaPept : a modern and open framework for MS-based proteomics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747666","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Receptor-interacting serine/threonine-protein kinase 1 (RIPK1) functions as a critical stress sentinel that coordinates cell survival, inflammation, and immunogenic cell death (ICD). Although the catalytic function of RIPK1 is required to trigger cell death, its non-catalytic scaffold function mediates strong pro-survival signaling. Accordingly, cancer cells can hijack RIPK1 to block necroptosis and evade immune detection. We generated a small-molecule proteolysis-targeting chimera (PROTAC) that selectively degraded human and murine RIPK1. PROTAC-mediated depletion of RIPK1 deregulated TNFR1 and TLR3/4 signaling hubs, accentuating the output of NF-κB, MAPK, and IFN signaling. Additionally, RIPK1 degradation simultaneously promoted RIPK3 activation and necroptosis induction. We further demonstrated that RIPK1 degradation enhanced the immunostimulatory effects of radio- and immunotherapy by sensitizing cancer cells to treatment-induced TNF and interferons. This promoted ICD, antitumor immunity, and durable treatment responses. Consequently, targeting RIPK1 by PROTACs emerges as a promising approach to overcome radio- or immunotherapy resistance and enhance anticancer therapies.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Mannion, Jonathan","Gifford, Valentina","Bellenie, Benjamin","Fernando, Winnie","Ramos Garcia, Laura","Wilson, Rebecca","John, Sidonie Wicky","Udainiya, Savita","Patin, Emmanuel C.","Tiu, Crescens","Smith, Angel","Goicoechea, Maria","Craxton, Andrew","Moraes de Vasconcelos, Nathalia","Guppy, Naomi","Cheung, Kwai Ming J.","Cundy, Nicholas J.","Pierrat, Olivier","Brennan, Alfie","Roumeliotis, Theodoros I.","Benstead-Hume, Graeme","Alexander, John","Muirhead, Gareth","Layzell, Scott","Lyu, Wenxin","Roulstone, Victoria","Allen, Mark","Baldock, Holly","Legrand, Arnaud","Gabel, Florian","Serrano-Aparicio, Natalia","Starling, Chris","Guo, Hongyan","Upton, Jason","Gyrd-Hansen, Mads","MacFarlane, Marion","Seddon, Benedict","Raynaud, Florence","Roxanis, Ioannis","Harrington, Kevin","Haider, Syed","Choudhary, Jyoti S.","Hoelder, Swen","Tenev, Tencho","Meier, Pascal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-749272"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Auburn University","Louisiana State University in Shreveport","The Institute of Cancer Research, London","University College London","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Cell Death","Immunotherapy","Inflammation","Interferon","Necroptosis","RIPK1","Radiotherapy","TLR3","TNF"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a ripk000000000001 specific protac degrader achieves potent antitumor activity by enhancing immunogenic cell death","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2024.04.025","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-749272","identifier":[{"id":"38788712","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11236506","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195286501","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-db10cb4c-1604-4a20-81cd-6453277bbf7d"],"keyword":["RIPK1","TLR3","TNF","anticancer immunity","cell death","immunotherapy","inflammation","interferon","necroptosis","radiotherapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A2ACFFD205C03CBFC566E294739D4F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/397992958/A_RIPK1_specific_PROTAC.htm","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.immuni.2024.04.025","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":