{"abstract":"Structural linguistic features are often overlooked yet potentially important aspects of journalistic practice. Especially in news reporting on climate change, these features can play a crucial role as the proper use of language is tied to message credibility, processing fluency and knowledge retention, which can positively influence the reader to take more climate action. This article analyzes language use in Danish news articles on climate change using a sample of around 32,000 articles from four different outlet types (quality news, niche papers, tabloids, and public service broadcasters) published from 1990 to 2021. We create a machine-learning model of text complexity covering this concept's semantic and syntactic dimensions. Our findings confirm expected differences in complexity between news outlets, highlighting tabloid articles as engaging with higher semantic complexity, while quality papers and niche papers exhibit higher syntactic complexity. We observe a significant decrease in semantic complexity and a slight increase in syntactic complexity over time, a trend towards more generic language, and an increased use of pronouns, verbs, and adverbs. Most of these changes can be attributed to the emergence of articles by public service broadcasters. Articles by public service broadcasters are characterised by high syntactic complexity, which we consider problematic due to their popularity among the general public.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian","Eskjær, Mikkel Fugl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726461"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-31","place":"Reykjavik, is","start":"2024-05-27","title":"Digital Humanities in the Nordic and Baltic Countries","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Climate change","Machine learning","Newspaper","Text complexity"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of textual complexity in danish news articles on climate change","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5617/dhnbpub.11490","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-726461","ids":["aau-fa2b2186-ccfe-4d13-aeeb-2ce3a7529012"],"keyword":["climate change","machine learning","newspaper","text complexity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DEBA036EC3428476F330BEC5005399E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/694923605/DHN2024_TextComplexity.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5617/dhnbpub.11490","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel","key":"eskjærpau","last":"Eskjær","locid":"7d28f13d-dfeb-474d-ba21-62b320ff2441","name":"Eskjær, Mikkel Fugl","name_org":"Eskjær, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-9979-1989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5617/dhnbpub.11490","issn":["27041441"],"issue":"1","publisher":"University of Oslo","series":"Digital Humanities in the Nordic and Baltic Countries Publications","status":"p","subtitle":"Digital Humanities in the Nordic and Baltic Countries 8th Conference","title":"Conference Proceedings of DHNB 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-fa2b2186-ccfe-4d13-aeeb-2ce3a7529012"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Analysis of Textual Complexity in Danish News Articles on Climate Change","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726461","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This chapter explores methodological aspects of collaborative ethnographic knowledge production. Ethnography, inherently collaborative, raises methodological questions related to the social, linguistic, spatial and national situatedness of research. The authors delve into the innovative potentials of transnational collaborative formats that extend beyond individual projects and national borders, aiming to connect diverse disciplinary, theoretical and regional traditions. It is argued that such collaboration permits the exploration of cultural forms beyond single sites, aligned to ‘multiscale ethnography’. It is discussed how collaborative efforts can reexplore ethnographic material already collected and how this can contribute to the development of new insights. Three overarching aspects emerge: first, the challenge of sharing knowledge in transnational collaborations, acknowledging the complexities of different local, national, methodological and theoretical communities. Second, the creation of new knowledge, illustrated through one project drafting alternative futures for universities and another one describing a bricolage resulting from re- and deconstruction processes. Third, the need to address general methodological questions and advance collective conceptualisations and understandings, emphasising the importance of developing an overarching community of practice and dealing with difference and uncertainty. Overall, the chapter aims to advance methodological reflection through a combination of concrete project contexts and general considerations.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Frank, Magnus","Egger, Anja Sieber","Unterweger, Gisela","Weitkämper, Florian","Wieser, Clemens","Wright, Susan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-708759"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ETH Zürich","University of Education Freiburg","University of Flensburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"elaborating new insights in transnational ethnographic collaborations opportunities and challenges","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781032629384-14","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-708759","identifier":[{"id":"85204859714","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a1e5cf2c-3750-4aa2-9f2e-7788c8eff7a7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A3ACB724F63710A30AF19C51593328DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4324/9781032629384-14","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of flensburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Flensburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"eth zürich","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"ETH Zürich","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of education freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Education Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - General Education and Educational Philosophy, Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus","key":"frankpau","last":"Frank","name":"Frank, Magnus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anja Sieber","key":"eggerpau","last":"Egger","name":"Egger, Anja Sieber","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gisela","key":"unterwegerpau","last":"Unterweger","name":"Unterweger, Gisela","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Florian","key":"weitkämperpau","last":"Weitkämper","name":"Weitkämper, Florian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Clemens","key":"wieserpau","last":"Wieser","locid":"5784d41d-97d9-4b06-867a-eea1cbb8ea65","name":"Wieser, Clemens","orcid":"0000-0003-3594-2789","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Susan","key":"wrightpau","last":"Wright","locid":"dac60d3f-f220-4991-bde2-4b7bc84e8362","name":"Wright, Susan","orcid":"0000-0002-8124-4335","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jürgen","key":"buddepedh","last":"Budde","name":"Budde, Jürgen","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anke","key":"wischmannpedh","last":"Wischmann","name":"Wischmann, Anke","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"meierpedh","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Michael","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Georg","key":"rißlerpedh","last":"Rißler","name":"Rißler, Georg","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4324/9781032629384-14","eisbn":["9781040124321","9781032629384"],"isbn":["9781032617350"],"pages":"135-151","place":"London","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","subtitle":"European Perspectives","title":"Novelty, Innovation and Transformation in Educational Ethnographic Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204859714"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a1e5cf2c-3750-4aa2-9f2e-7788c8eff7a7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Elaborating New Insights in Transnational Ethnographic Collaborations : Opportunities and Challenges","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-708759","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Addressing the climate crisis calls for global efforts to mitigate greenhouse gas emissions, with effective mitigation efforts depending on an informed public with a high degree of climate change awareness. This study examines global engagement with climate change and related concepts through an analysis of around 517 Million Wikipedia pageviews of 3965 items from WikiProject Climate Change across 213 countries in the years 2017 to 2022. We take advantage of Wikimedia Foundation's differentially-private daily pageview dataset, which makes it possible to study Wikipedia viewing behavior in a language edition agnostic way and on a per-country basis. Temporal analysis reveals a stagnant engagement with climate change articles, contrary to societal trends, possibly due to the attitude-behavior gap. We also found substantial regional differences, with countries from the global north displaying greater traffic compared to the global south. Specific events, notably Greta Thunberg's speech at the UN climate summit in 2019, drive peaks in climate change engagement, highlighting the social dimension and influence of prominent figures in climate change information seeking. However, causal time series analyses show that events like these do not lead to long-lasting increased traffic.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-717102"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-24","place":"Stuttgart, de","start":"2024-05-21","title":"16th ACM Web Science Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Climate change","Public Interest","Time series analysis","Wikipedia"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using wikipedia pageview data to investigate public interest in climate change at a global scale","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3614419.3644007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-717102","identifier":[{"id":"85195143261","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f99e36e3-ed7a-4980-8152-6d25adb51271"],"keyword":["Climate Change","Public Interest","TIme Series Analysis","Wikipedia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF25B4986CEFB0956D94366250254578"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/700708326/Meier_Wiki_Climate.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3614419.3644007","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Luca Maria","key":"aiellopedh","last":"Aiello","name":"Aiello, Luca Maria","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Yelena","key":"mejovapedh","last":"Mejova","name":"Mejova, Yelena","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Oshani","key":"seneviratnepedh","last":"Seneviratne","name":"Seneviratne, Oshani","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jun","key":"sunpedh","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Jun","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sierra","key":"kaiserpedh","last":"Kaiser","name":"Kaiser, Sierra","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Steffen","key":"staabpedh","last":"Staab","name":"Staab, Steffen","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3614419.3644007","eisbn":["9798400703348"],"pages":"365-375","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 16th ACM Web Science Conference","title":"WebSci 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195143261"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f99e36e3-ed7a-4980-8152-6d25adb51271"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Using Wikipedia Pageview Data to Investigate Public Interest in Climate Change at a Global Scale","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-717102","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The terms greenhouse effect, global warming, and climate change are often used synonymously in everyday conversations about the warming planet. Utilizing Danish BERT, the study employs masked language model tasks to uncover semantic shifts and variations of these climate change-related keywords in Danish news articles from 1990 to 2021. The findings offer insights into contextual understandings and framing nuances by journalists, contributing to a deeper comprehension of these terms in the Danish media discourse on CC.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736029"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using bert to study semantic variations of climate change keywords in danish news articles","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/698099033/DHN2024_KeywordsMASK.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-736029","ids":["aau-6d52bfb8-d334-4db4-8e4e-8d9512912786"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-458FD70170B492A4973439B4CE0665F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/698099033/DHN2024_KeywordsMASK.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Poster @ DHNB 2024 Digital Humanities in the Nordic and Baltic Countries 8th Conference"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-6d52bfb8-d334-4db4-8e4e-8d9512912786"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Using BERT to Study Semantic Variations of Climate Change Keywords in Danish News Articles","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-736029","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Climate change is a dynamic and rapidly evolving media agenda. First associated with scientific notions of the greenhouse effect, it was later presented as global warming before reaching the current and broader picture of climate change. Over its development, climate change reporting has touched on a broad range of topics reflecting shifting scientific understandings, political interventions, and public anxieties, all of which condition the public's view and actions on climate change. To better understand which issues the Danish public has been exposed to, this study uses topic modeling to analyse 32 years of climate change communication in Denmark (1990–2021, n = 63,743). It identifies 85 topics grouped into 14 themes dealing with climate change in Danish national media outlets. Topics differ in prevalence and longitudinal stability while reflecting outlet bias in political leaning and communicative modalities. The most pronounced differences in climate change reporting are between public service media and traditional newspapers. This indicates that media users relying mainly on online news from public service providers, without additional access to print media, will receive information on climate change that is more topical and less politicized, more thematic and less structural, more about high-level politics than everyday interventions and more concerned with consequences than solutions.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian","Eskjær, Mikkel Fugl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-716608"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Meier, Florian Maximilian"],"keyword":["Climate change","Content analysis","News media","Topic modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"topic modeling three decades of climate change news in denmark","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcomm.2023.1322498","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The author(s) declare that no financial support was received for the research, authorship, and/or publication of this article."],"id":"S01-000.00-716608","identifier":[{"id":"85182715094","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0d06d773-473f-4165-8428-02a65f79ed85"],"keyword":["climate change","content analysis","news media","outlet bias","topic modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EDEFD513A800E89E03DD12ECDCCE72FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcomm.2023.1322498","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/645952546/fcomm-08-1322498.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human Centered Science and Digital Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","name_org":"Meier, Florian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Fugl","key":"eskjærpau","last":"Eskjær","locid":"7d28f13d-dfeb-474d-ba21-62b320ff2441","name":"Eskjær, Mikkel Fugl","orcid":"0000-0001-9979-1989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fcomm.2023.1322498","issn":["2297900X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Communication","paperid":"1322498","publisher":"Frontiers Media","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Communication","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182715094"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0d06d773-473f-4165-8428-02a65f79ed85"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Topic modeling three decades of climate change news in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-716608","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Cellular functions are mediated by protein-protein interactions, and mapping the interactome provides fundamental insights into biological systems. Affinity purification coupled to mass spectrometry is an ideal tool for such mapping, but it has been difficult to identify low copy number complexes, membrane complexes and complexes that are disrupted by protein tagging. As a result, our current knowledge of the interactome is far from complete, and assessing the reliability of reported interactions is challenging. Here we develop a sensitive high-throughput method using highly reproducible affinity enrichment coupled to mass spectrometry combined with a quantitative two-dimensional analysis strategy to comprehensively map the interactome of Saccharomyces cerevisiae. Thousand-fold reduced volumes in 96-well format enabled replicate analysis of the endogenous GFP-tagged library covering the entire expressed yeast proteome1. The 4,159 pull-downs generated a highly structured network of 3,927 proteins connected by 31,004 interactions, doubling the number of proteins and tripling the number of reliable interactions compared with existing interactome maps2. This includes very-low-abundance epigenetic complexes, organellar membrane complexes and non-taggable complexes inferred by abundance correlation. This nearly saturated interactome reveals that the vast majority of yeast proteins are highly connected, with an average of 16 interactors. Similar to social networks between humans, the average shortest distance between proteins is 4.2 interactions. AlphaFold-Multimer provided novel insights into the functional roles of previously uncharacterized proteins in complexes. Our web portal ( www.yeast-interactome.org ) enables extensive exploration of the interactome dataset.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Michaelis, André C","Brunner, Andreas-David","Zwiebel, Maximilian","Meier, Florian","Strauss, Maximilian T.","Bludau, Isabell","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719505"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["Databases Factual","Epigenesis Genetic","Mass spectrometry","Protein Interaction Maps","Proteome chemistry","Reproducibility of Results","Saccharomyces cerevisiae chemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the social and structural architecture of the yeast protein interactome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06739-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719505","identifier":[{"id":"001105882300009","type":"wos"},{"id":"85176557666","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10700138","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37968396","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1f69068c-d42e-43f0-bf6f-dcd8373d1571"],"keyword":["Databases, Factual","Epigenesis, Genetic","Mass Spectrometry","Protein Interaction Mapping/methods","Protein Interaction Maps","Proteome/chemistry","Reproducibility of Results","Saccharomyces cerevisiae Proteins/chemistry","Saccharomyces cerevisiae/chemistry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D373D20559B62F17C73B7DED30F360C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-023-06739-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379170104/s41586_023_06739_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of 