"The social and structural architecture of the yeast protein interactome","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719505","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Governments and organizations often offer cash payments for vaccination. How effective are such payments? A literature review shows that incentives usually increase vaccination, especially for nonhesitant populations and when using guaranteed payments. Concerns about negative unintended consequences are unsupported. We also discuss open questions and avenues for future research.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schneider, Florian H.","Campos-Mercade, Pol","Meier, Armando","Pope, Devin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721679"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"motivating vaccination with financial incentives","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tics.2023.07.003","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721679","identifier":[{"id":"85171267038","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37716894","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-bb80af9c-16fd-4f6e-badd-8d90fb84f270"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-37C3EEEB0CAF97447C674A1FE8048B3B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tics.2023.07.003","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375968965/1_s2.0_S1364661323001717_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Economics, Department of Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Florian Hans Fred","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"214a624d-2f75-4637-8672-48e63f5bb2f5","name":"Schneider, Florian H.","name_org":"Schneider, Florian Hans Fred","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pol","key":"camposmercadepau","last":"Campos-Mercade","name":"Campos-Mercade, Pol","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Armando","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Armando","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Devin","key":"popepau","last":"Pope","name":"Pope, Devin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37716894"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tics.2023.07.003","issn":["13646613","1879307X"],"issn_org":["13646613"],"issue":"12","journal":"Trends in Cognitive Sciences","pages":"1099-1101","status":"p","title":"Trends in Cognitive Sciences","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171267038"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-bb80af9c-16fd-4f6e-badd-8d90fb84f270"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Motivating vaccination with financial incentives","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721679","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Data-independent acquisition (DIA) methods have become increasingly popular in mass spectrometry (MS)-based proteomics because they enable continuous acquisition of fragment spectra for all precursors simultaneously. However, these advantages come with the challenge of correctly reconstructing the precursor-fragment relationships in these highly convoluted spectra for reliable identification and quantification. Here we introduce a scan mode for the combination of trapped ion mobility spectrometry (TIMS) with parallel accumulation - serial fragmentation (PASEF) that seamlessly and continuously follows the natural shape of the ion cloud in ion mobility and peptide precursor mass dimensions. Termed synchro-PASEF, it increases the detected fragment ion current several-fold at sub-second cycle times. Consecutive quadrupole selection windows move synchronously through the mass and ion mobility range. In this process, the quadrupole slices through the peptide precursors, which separates fragment ion signals of each precursor into adjacent synchro-PASEF scans. This precisely defines precursor - fragment relationships in ion mobility and mass dimensions and effectively deconvolutes the DIA fragment space. Importantly, the partitioned parts of the fragment ion transitions provide a further dimension of specificity via a lock and key mechanism. This is also advantageous for quantification, where signals from interfering precursors in the DIA selection window do not affect all partitions of the fragment ion, allowing to retain only the specific parts for quantification. Overall, we establish the defining features of synchro-PASEF and explore its potential for proteomic analyses.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Skowronek, Patricia","Krohs, Florian","Lubeck, Markus","Wallmann, Georg","Itang, Ericka C M","Koval, Polina","Wahle, Maria","Thielert, Marvin","Meier, Florian","Willems, Sander","Raether, Oliver","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-457558"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bruker Daltonics GmbH & Co. KG (Biz)","Jena University Hospital","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Kyiv Academic University"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synchro pasef allows precursor specific fragment ion extraction and interference removal in data independent acquisition","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100489","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-457558","identifier":[{"id":"85148678304","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001002526000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9868879","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36566012","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6b63b3b2-5cc3-42cc-813f-a62b03418f4c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E13D57F215FA6FC0CC66D4A810B8156B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/357770696/1_s2.0_S1535947622002973_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100489","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"bruker daltonics gmbh co kg","name":"Bruker Daltonics GmbH & Co. KG (Biz)","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Kyiv Academic University"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"jena university hospital","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Jena University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Mann Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Patricia","key":"skowronekpau","last":"Skowronek","name":"Skowronek, Patricia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Florian","key":"krohspau","last":"Krohs","name":"Krohs, Florian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Markus","key":"lubeckpau","last":"Lubeck","name":"Lubeck, Markus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Georg","key":"wallmannpau","last":"Wallmann","name":"Wallmann, Georg","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ericka C M","key":"itangpau","last":"Itang","name":"Itang, Ericka C M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Polina","key":"kovalpau","last":"Koval","name":"Koval, Polina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"wahlepau","last":"Wahle","name":"Wahle, Maria","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marvin","key":"thielertpau","last":"Thielert","name":"Thielert, Marvin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sander","key":"willemspau","last":"Willems","name":"Willems, Sander","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Oliver","key":"raetherpau","last":"Raether","name":"Raether, Oliver","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36566012"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100489","issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"issue":"2","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","paperid":"100489","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148678304"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6b63b3b2-5cc3-42cc-813f-a62b03418f4c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Synchro-PASEF allows precursor-specific fragment ion extraction and interference removal in data-independent acquisition","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-457558","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Financial incentives to encourage healthy and prosocial behaviours often trigger initial behavioural change1–11, but a large academic literature warns against using them12–16. Critics warn that financial incentives can crowd out prosocial motivations and reduce perceived safety and trust, thereby reducing healthy behaviours when no payments are offered and eroding morals more generally17–24. Here we report findings from a large-scale, pre-registered study in Sweden that causally measures the unintended consequences of offering financial incentives for taking the first dose of a COVID-19 vaccine. We use a unique combination of random exposure to financial incentives, population-wide administrative vaccination records and rich survey data. We find no negative consequences of financial incentives; we can reject even small negative impacts of offering financial incentives on future vaccination uptake, morals, trust and perceived safety. In a complementary study, we find that informing US residents about the existence of state incentive programmes also has no negative consequences. Our findings inform not only the academic debate on financial incentives for behaviour change but also policy-makers who consider using financial incentives to change behaviour.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Schneider, Florian H.","Campos-Mercade, Pol","Meier, Stephan","Pope, Devin","Wengström, Erik Roland","Meier, Armando N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721199"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Columbia University","National Bureau of Economic Research","The University of Chicago","University of Basel","University of Lausanne"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"financial incentives for vaccination do not have negative unintended consequences","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05512-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721199","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9833033","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36631607","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146081463","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-97c6adac-560a-49d2-b68f-1730cbd6b394"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-304C12DE6718AE6EB1AD7306FBCDC7E3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/375968180/s41586_022_05512_4.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05512-4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Economics, Department of Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"columbia university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Columbia University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"the university of chicago","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"The University of Chicago","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"national bureau of economic research","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"National Bureau of Economic Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"ch","key":"university of lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"ch","key":"university of basel","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Basel","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Florian H.","key":"schneiderflorianhpau","last":"Schneider","locid":"214a624d-2f75-4637-8672-48e63f5bb2f5","name":"Schneider, Florian H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pol","key":"camposmercadepolpau","last":"Campos-Mercade","locid":"404b6d52-5463-46b4-88d4-064b3a1167b0","name":"Campos-Mercade, Pol","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stephan","key":"meierstephanpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Stephan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Devin","key":"popedevinpau","last":"Pope","name":"Pope, Devin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erik","key":"wengströmerikrolandpau","last":"Wengström","locid":"338b0198-6eee-45a9-bc74-fbfc11593edf","name":"Wengström, Erik Roland","name_org":"Wengström, Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","first":"Armando N.","key":"meierarmandonpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Armando N.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36631607"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-022-05512-4","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"journal":"Nature","pages":"526-533","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"613"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146081463"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-97c6adac-560a-49d2-b68f-1730cbd6b394"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Financial incentives for vaccination do not have negative unintended consequences","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721199","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Mathematics education is like many scientific disciplines witnessing an increase in scientific output. Examining and reviewing every paper in an area in detail are time-consuming, making comprehensive reviews a challenging task. Unsupervised machine learning algorithms like topic models have become increasingly popular in recent years. Their ability to summarize large amounts of unstructured text into coherent themes or topics allows researchers in any field to keep an overview of state of the art by creating automated literature reviews. In this article, we apply topic modeling in the context of mathematics education and showcase the use of this data science approach for creating literature reviews by training a model of all papers (n = 336) that have been presented in Thematic Working Groups related to technology in the first eleven Congresses of the European Society for Research in Mathematics Education (CERME). We guide the reader through the stepwise process of training a model and give recommendations for best practices and decisions that are decisive for the success of such an approach to a literature review. We find that research in this period revolved around 25 distinct topics that can be grouped into four clusters: digital tools, teachers and their resources, technology experimentation, and a diverse cluster with a strong focus on student activity. Finally, a temporal analysis of these topics reveals a correlation between technology trends and research focus, allowing for reflection on future research in the field.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Dreyøe, Jonas","Tamborg, Andreas Lindenskov","Meier, Florian","Allsopp, Benjamin Brink","Misfeldt, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-098.67-011789"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Herfort, Jonas Dreyøe"],"keyword":["Digital technology","Literature review","Topic modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000020 years of research on technology in mathematics education at cerme a literature review based on a data science approach","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/428316642/20_years_of_research_on_technology_in_mathematics_education_at_CERME1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-098.67-011789","identifier":[{"id":"85145604216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f6b731c8-2bea-432c-bf40-5789d59e77cc","ku-f7790c64-18d5-400b-ab40-a4abdaed09cf"],"keyword":["Digital technology","Educational data science","Literature review","Topic modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DF71D5828635FB6A6A9CF72255EFE4A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/709473760/ESM-CERME.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/428316642/20_years_of_research_on_technology_in_mathematics_education_at_CERME1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Didactics of Information and Communication Technology (ICT) in Science Education","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Science Education, Didactics of Mathematics"],"nora_co