{"abstract":"Authorship attribution is performed on a comparative basis where a text's style is compared to a possible authors candidate's style. Picking the right candidates, however, is not always a straightforward task. By performing a stylistic characterisation of authors, we present three different steps that can support this candidate selection process.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-096358"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Authorship Attribution","Text mining","Trykkefrihedstiden"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards authorship attribution in the trykkefrihedsskrifter a stylistic analysis of the danish freedom of the press writings main writers","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-096358","ids":["aau-9fc9e658-60fd-46a4-ae15-2abd14dde6fc"],"keyword":["Authorship Attribution","Stylistic Analysis","Text Mining","Trykkefrihedstiden"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-74FD2B8528885F6CF69C8C40AFAE5AAC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"u","title":"pre-print"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Unpublished"]},"sid":["aau-9fc9e658-60fd-46a4-ae15-2abd14dde6fc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Towards Authorship Attribution in the Trykkefrihedsskrifter: A Stylistic Analysis of the Danish Freedom of the Press Writings’ Main Writers","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-096358","year":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Data-independent acquisition (DIA) methods have become increasingly attractive in mass spectrometry-based proteomics because they enable high data completeness and a wide dynamic range. Recently, we combined DIA with parallel accumulation-serial fragmentation (dia-PASEF) on a Bruker trapped ion mobility (IM) separated quadrupole time-of-flight mass spectrometer. This requires alignment of the IM separation with the downstream mass selective quadrupole, leading to a more complex scheme for dia-PASEF window placement compared with DIA. To achieve high data completeness and deep proteome coverage, here we employ variable isolation windows that are placed optimally depending on precursor density in the m/z and IM plane. This is implemented in the freely available py_diAID (Python package for DIA with an automated isolation design) package. In combination with in-depth project-specific proteomics libraries and the Evosep liquid chromatography system, we reproducibly identified over 7700 proteins in a human cancer cell line in 44 min with quadruplicate single-shot injections at high sensitivity. Even at a throughput of 100 samples per day (11 min liquid chromatography gradients), we consistently quantified more than 6000 proteins in mammalian cell lysates by injecting four replicates. We found that optimal dia-PASEF window placement facilitates in-depth phosphoproteomics with very high sensitivity, quantifying more than 35,000 phosphosites in a human cancer cell line stimulated with an epidermal growth factor in triplicate 21 min runs. This covers a substantial part of the regulated phosphoproteome with high sensitivity, opening up for extensive systems-biological studies.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Skowronek, Patricia","Thielert, Marvin","Voytik, Eugenia","Tanzer, Maria C","Hansen, Fynn M","Willems, Sander","Karayel, Ozge","Brunner, Andreas-David","Meier, Florian","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-490336"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["Animals","Chromatography Liquid methods","Epidermal Growth Factor","Humans","Mammals metabolism","Proteome metabolism","Proteomics methods","Tandem Mass Spectrometry methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rapid and in depth coverage of the phospho proteome with deep libraries and optimal window design for dia pasef","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100279","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-490336","identifier":[{"id":"35944843","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138645433","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000863182900001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC9465115","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a22049b2-a4ed-47d2-b7b2-ad7dad512b71"],"keyword":["Animals","Chromatography, Liquid/methods","Epidermal Growth Factor","Humans","Mammals/metabolism","Proteome/metabolism","Proteomics/methods","Tandem Mass Spectrometry/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D9BEB1C5F0F38B93542D7E9469BEC9CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100279","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321962504/1_s2.0_S1535947622000871_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Mann Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Patricia","key":"skowronekpau","last":"Skowronek","name":"Skowronek, Patricia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marvin","key":"thielertpau","last":"Thielert","name":"Thielert, Marvin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eugenia","key":"voytikpau","last":"Voytik","name":"Voytik, Eugenia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria C","key":"tanzerpau","last":"Tanzer","name":"Tanzer, Maria C","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Fynn M","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Fynn M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sander","key":"willemspau","last":"Willems","name":"Willems, Sander","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ozge","key":"karayelpau","last":"Karayel","name":"Karayel, Ozge","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas-David","key":"brunnerpau","last":"Brunner","name":"Brunner, Andreas-David","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35944843"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcpro.2022.100279","issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"issue":"9","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","paperid":"100279","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138645433"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a22049b2-a4ed-47d2-b7b2-ad7dad512b71"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rapid and In-Depth Coverage of the (Phospho-)Proteome With Deep Libraries and Optimal Window Design for dia-PASEF","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-490336","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Recent research has shown how strongly connected Wikipedia and other web applications are. For example, search engines rely heavily on surfacing Wikipedia links to satisfy their users' information needs and volunteer-created Wikipedia content frequently gets re-used on social media platforms like Reddit. However, publicly accessible datasets that enable researchers to study the interrelationship between Wikipedia and other platforms are sparse. In addition to that, most studies only focus on certain points in time and do not consider the historical perspective. To begin solving these problems, we developed TWikiL, the Twitter Wikipedia Link Dataset, which contains all Wikipedia links posted on Twitter in the period 2006 to January 2021. We extract Wikipedia links from Tweets and enrich the referenced articles with their respective Wikidata identifiers and Wikipedia topic categories. This makes the dataset immediately useful for a large range of scholarly use cases. In this paper, we describe the data collection process, perform an initial exploratory analysis and present a comprehensive overview of how this dataset can be useful for the research community.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-053302"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Open data","Twitter","Wikipedia"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"twikil the twitter wikipedia link dataset","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1609/icwsm.v16i1.19381","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-053302","ids":["aau-0b349857-4051-4d9c-8c3a-0d021ccc0626"],"keyword":["Cross-platform analysis","Open Data","Twitter","Wikipedia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F21CF921802BEE6FF7B3A73D64A9DEFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1609/icwsm.v16i1.19381","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/469254677/ICWSM22_TWikiL.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Human-centered AI","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Purposeful Technology Lab","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, MASSHINE","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, AI for the People"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian Maximilian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1609/icwsm.v16i1.19381","pages":"1292","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of ICWSM 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0b349857-4051-4d9c-8c3a-0d021ccc0626"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"TWikiL - The Twitter Wikipedia Link Dataset","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-053302","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
