last":"Brunner","name":"Brunner, Andreas-David","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Stephanie","key":"kasparschoenefeldpau","last":"Kaspar-Schoenefeld","name":"Kaspar-Schoenefeld, Stephanie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Scarlet","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, Scarlet","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Markus","key":"lubeckpau","last":"Lubeck","name":"Lubeck, Markus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Oliver","key":"raetherpau","last":"Raether","name":"Raether, Oliver","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ben C.","key":"collinspau","last":"Collins","name":"Collins, Ben C.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ruedi","key":"aebersoldpau","last":"Aebersold","name":"Aebersold, Ruedi","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hannes","key":"rostpau","last":"Rost","name":"Rost, Hannes","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"issue":"8","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","title_org":"Molecular & Cellular Proteomics","volume":"18"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b130897b-b316-4de5-a98c-a62570506628"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Mobi-DIK (Ion Mobility DIA Analysis Kit): Targeted analysis software for diaPASEF data improves proteome coverage","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499272","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In bottom-up proteomics, peptides are separated by liquid chromatography with elution peak widths in the range of seconds, while mass spectra are acquired in about 100 microseconds with time-of-flight (TOF) instruments. This allows adding ion mobility as a third dimension of separation. Among several formats, trapped ion mobility spectrometry (TIMS) is attractive due to its small size, low voltage requirements and high efficiency of ion utilization. We have recently demonstrated a scan mode termed parallel accumulation - serial fragmentation (PASEF), which multiplies the sequencing speed without any loss in sensitivity (Meier et al., PMID: 26538118). Here we introduce the timsTOF Pro instrument, which optimally implements online PASEF. It features an orthogonal ion path into the ion mobility device, limiting the amount of debris entering the instrument and making it very robust in daily operation. We investigate different precursor selection schemes for shotgun proteomics to optimally allocate in excess of 100 fragmentation events per second. More than 600,000 fragmentation spectra in standard 120 min LC runs are achievable, which can be used for near exhaustive precursor selection in complex mixtures or accumulating the signal of weak precursors. In 120 min single runs of HeLa digest, MaxQuant identified more than 6,000 proteins in single run HeLa analyses without matching to a library, and with high quantitative reproducibility (R > 0.97). Online PASEF achieves a remarkable sensitivity with more than 2,500 proteins identified in 30 min runs of only 10 ng HeLa digest. We also show that highly reproducible collisional cross sections can be acquired on a large scale (R > 0.99). PASEF on the timsTOF Pro is a valuable addition to the technological toolbox in proteomics, with a number of unique operating modes that are only beginning to be explored.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Meier, Florian","Brunner, Andreas-David","Koch, Scarlet","Koch, Heiner","Lubeck, Markus","Krause, Michael","Goedecke, Niels","Decker, Jens","Kosinski, Thomas","Park, Melvin A","Bache, Nicolai","Hoerning, Ole","Cox, Jürgen","Räther, Oliver","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421295"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bruker Daltonik GmbH","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Bruker Daltonics Inc., United States of America."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"online parallel accumulation serial fragmentation pasef with a novel trapped ion mobility mass spectrometer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.TIR118.000900","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-421295","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6283298","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85057756562","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30385480","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2ec5e842-4340-4b70-9067-2f551805d162"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4DBC16E7B89926E8EA9BFF5678B368C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/218082151/2534.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.TIR118.000900","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"bruker daltonik gmbh","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bruker Daltonik GmbH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Bruker Daltonics Inc., United States of America."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Florian","key":"meierflorianpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas-David","key":"brunnerandreasdavidpau","last":"Brunner","name":"Brunner, Andreas-David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Scarlet","key":"kochscarletpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, Scarlet","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Heiner","key":"kochheinerpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, Heiner","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Markus","key":"lubeckmarkuspau","last":"Lubeck","name":"Lubeck, Markus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"krausemichaelpau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"goedeckenielspau","last":"Goedecke","name":"Goedecke, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"deckerjenspau","last":"Decker","name":"Decker, Jens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"kosinskithomaspau","last":"Kosinski","name":"Kosinski, Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Melvin A","key":"parkmelvinapau","last":"Park","name":"Park, Melvin A","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nicolai","key":"bachenicolaipau","last":"Bache","name":"Bache, Nicolai","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ole","key":"hoerningolepau","last":"Hoerning","name":"Hoerning, Ole","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jürgen","key":"coxjürgenpau","last":"Cox","name":"Cox, Jürgen","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Oliver","key":"rätheroliverpau","last":"Räther","name":"Räther, Oliver","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Matthias","key":"mannmatthiaspau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30385480"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/mcp.tir118.000900","issn":["15359476","15359484"],"issn_org":["15359476"],"issue":"12","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","pages":"2534-2545","status":"p","title":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057756562"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2ec5e842-4340-4b70-9067-2f551805d162"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Online parallel accumulation - serial fragmentation (PASEF) with a novel trapped ion mobility mass spectrometer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421295","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"To further integrate mass spectrometry (MS)-based proteomics into biomedical research and especially into clinical settings, high throughput and robustness are essential requirements. They are largely met in high-flow rate chromatographic systems for small molecules but these are not sufficiently sensitive for proteomics applications. Here we describe a new concept that delivers on these requirements while maintaining the sensitivity of current nano-flow LC systems. Low-pressure pumps elute the sample from a disposable trap column, simultaneously forming a chromatographic gradient that is stored in a long storage loop. An auxiliary gradient creates an offset, ensuring the re-focusing of the peptides before the separation on the analytical column by a single high-pressure pump. This simplified design enables robust operation over thousands of sample injections. Furthermore, the steps between injections are performed in parallel, reducing overhead time to a few minutes and allowing analysis of more than 200 samples per day. From fractionated HeLa cell lysates, deep proteomes covering more than 130,000 sequence unique peptides and close to 10,000 proteins were rapidly acquired. Using this data as a library, we demonstrate quantitation of 5200 proteins in only 21 min. Thus, the new system - termed Evosep One - analyzes samples in an extremely robust and high throughput manner, without sacrificing in depth proteomics coverage.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bache, Nicolai","Geyer, Philipp E.","Bekker-Jensen, Dorte B.","Hørning, Ole","Falkenby, Lasse","Treit, Peter V.","Doll, Sophia","Paron, Igor","Müller, Johannes B.","Meier, Florian","Olsen, Jesper V.","Vorm, Ole","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-514789"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel lc system embeds analytes in pre formed gradients for rapid ultra robust proteomics","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.TIR118.000853","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-514789","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6210218","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30104208","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85055910107","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-cb34c39c-efa6-42ae-8124-1054e1ed783b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE0090DA417453FC6A693E2600D2E175"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/mcp.TIR118.000853","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/210007573/2284.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Evosep Biosystems (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai","key":"bachepau","last":"Bache","name":"Bache, Nicolai","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Philipp E.","key":"geyerpau","last":"Geyer","locid":"fc9