L","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","evosep biosystems (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cb34c39c-efa6-42ae-8124-1054e1ed783b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A novel LC system embeds analytes in pre-formed gradients for rapid, ultra-robust proteomics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-514789","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"We developed EASI-tag (easily abstractable sulfoxide-based isobaric-tag), a new type of amine-derivatizing and sulfoxide-containing isobaric labeling reagents for highly accurate quantitative proteomics analysis using mass spectrometry. We observed that EASI-tag labels dissociate at low collision energy and generate peptide-coupled, interference-free reporter ions with high yield. Efficient isolation of 12C precursors and quantification at the MS2 level allowed accurate determination of quantitative differences between up to six multiplexed samples.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Virreira Winter, Sebastian","Meier, Florian","Wichmann, Christoph","Cox, Juergen","Mann, Matthias","Meissner, Felix"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-467599"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"easi tag enables accurate multiplexed and interference free ms000000000002 based proteome quantification","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-467599","identifier":[{"id":"85048656968","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29915187","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7bd475c5-c056-4472-a7ed-89ca06fc8060"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-579926015FFCA4976FA5EA8AF30B2C71"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian","key":"virreirawinterpau","last":"Virreira Winter","name":"Virreira Winter, Sebastian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christoph","key":"wichmannpau","last":"Wichmann","name":"Wichmann, Christoph","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juergen","key":"coxpau","last":"Cox","name":"Cox, Juergen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Felix","key":"meissnerpau","last":"Meissner","name":"Meissner, Felix","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29915187"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-018-0037-8","issn":["15487091","15487105"],"issn_org":["15487091"],"issue":"7","journal":"Nature Methods","pages":"527-530","status":"p","title":"Nature Methods","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048656968"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7bd475c5-c056-4472-a7ed-89ca06fc8060"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EASI-tag enables accurate multiplexed and interference-free MS2-based proteome quantification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-467599","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Great advances have been made in sensitivity and acquisition speed on the Orbitrap mass analyzer, enabling increasingly deep proteome coverage. However, these advances have been mainly limited to the MS2 level, whereas ion beam sampling for the MS1 scans remains extremely inefficient. Here we report a data-acquisition method, termed BoxCar, in which filling multiple narrow mass-to-charge segments increases the mean ion injection time more than tenfold as compared to that of a standard full scan. In 1-h analyses, the method provided MS1-level evidence for more than 90% of the proteome of a human cancer cell line that had previously been identified in 24 fractions, and it quantified more than 6,200 proteins in ten of ten replicates. In mouse brain tissue, we detected more than 10,000 proteins in only 100 min, and sensitivity extended into the low-attomolar range.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Meier, Florian","Geyer, Philipp E.","Virreira Winter, Sebastian","Cox, Juergen","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518224"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"boxcar acquisition method enables single shot proteomics at a depth of 000000000010 000000000000 proteins in 000000000100 minutes","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-518224","identifier":[{"id":"85046553783","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29735998","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d0d7bc53-12fc-418e-84cd-54067fe446d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A07659ED2D5F912CA731795D43FFAF78"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philipp E.","key":"geyerpau","last":"Geyer","locid":"fc987200-bf00-477b-8c57-e83a7984b89e","name":"Geyer, Philipp E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian","key":"virreirawinterpau","last":"Virreira Winter","name":"Virreira Winter, Sebastian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Juergen","key":"coxpau","last":"Cox","name":"Cox, Juergen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29735998"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-018-0003-5","issn":["15487091","15487105"],"issn_org":["15487091"],"issue":"6","journal":"Nature Methods","pages":"440-448","status":"p","title":"Nature Methods","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046553783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d0d7bc53-12fc-418e-84cd-54067fe446d9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"BoxCar acquisition method enables single-shot proteomics at a depth of 10,000 proteins in 100 minutes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518224","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Returning to previously viewed or possessed information — re-finding — is a core information seeking behaviour that has been studied in diverse contexts including physical environments, personal computer filing systems, web search and email. Despite being designed for real-time and ephemeral content, recent studies have shown that re-finding of older content is performed in social media applications too. To better understand why this is and how re-finding can be better supported, in this work we describe the results of a large-scale web-based survey which queried 606 Twitter users on how and how often they re-find, as well as the motivations for this behaviour. Our main contribution is the qualitative analysis of these motivations and motivations sourced via two existing studies, resulting in a coding scheme documenting the breadth and frequency of different social media re-finding tasks. We discuss how this classification can be used in (i) the design of task-based evaluations, (ii) the detection and interpretation of re-finding in click-stream data and (iii) the design of social media search systems.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Meier, Florian Maximilian","Elsweiler, David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086874"],"event":{"acronym":"CHIIR","end":"2018-03-15","place":"New Brunswick, us","start":"2018-03-11","title":"CHIIR 2018: 3rd ACM SIGIR Conference on Information Interaction and Retrieval","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Regensburg"],"keyword":["Personal Information Management","Re finding","Social media","Survey","Twitter"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"other times its just strolling back through my timeline investigating re finding behaviour on twitter and its motivations","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85052023301&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-086874","identifier":[{"id":"85052023301","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-7e9fbb7b-5ce2-40d5-8fd4-01c4df07a8cf"],"keyword":["Personal Information Management","Re-finding","Social Media","Survey","Twitter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3125A868C8295BBA4D6541CB34D87310"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Science, Policy and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of regensburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Regensburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","locid":"30784c17-7dc1-48de-9a36-f6e17f329de0","name":"Meier, Florian Maximilian","name_org":"Meier, Florian","orcid":"0000-0001-9408-0686","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"elsweilerpau","last":"Elsweiler","name":"Elsweiler, David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3176349.3176392","isbn":["9781450349253"],"pages":"130-139","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 Conference on Human Information Interaction Retrieval"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052023301"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-7e9fbb7b-5ce2-40d5-8fd4-01c4df07a8cf"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Other Times Its Just Strolling Back Through My Timeline: Investigating Re-finding Behaviour on Twitter and Its Motivations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-086874","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Obesity-related diseases affect half of the global population, and bariatric surgery is one of the few interventions with long-lasting weight loss and cardio-metabolic effects. Here, we investigated the effect of Roux-en-Y gastric bypass surgery on the plasma proteome, hypothesizing that specific proteins or protein patterns may serve as key mediators and markers of the metabolic response. We performed mass spectrometry (MS)-based proteomics on two longitudinal studies encompassing 47 morbidly obese patients, generating quantitative information on more than 1,700 proteins. A global correlation matrix incorporating about 200,000 relationships revealed functional connections between proteins and assigned them to physiological processes. The main classes of significantly altered proteins were markers of systemic inflammation and those involved in lipid metabolism. Our data highlight robust correlative and anti-correlative behaviors of circulating proteins to each other and to clinical parameters. A group of inflammation-related proteins showed distinct inverse relationships to proteins consistently associated with insulin sensitivity.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Geyer, Philipp E.","Doll, Sophia","Treit, Peter V","Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","Martinussen, Christoffer","Jørgensen, Nils B","Torekov, Signe Sørensen","Meier, Florian","Niu, Lili","Santos, Alberto","Keilhauer, Eva C","Holst, Jens Juul","Madsbad, Sten","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453382"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma proteome profiling reveals dynamics of inflammatory and lipid homeostasis markers after roux en y gastric bypass surgery","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cels.2018.10.012","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453382","identifier":[{"id":"30528273","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85059240341","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6445e470-eef1-4503-81f8-510861746fbb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5EECDE28B15EAC198D0D9A76CAC1B632"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/211216927/ArticleOpenAccess.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cels.2018.10.012","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Translational Metabolic Physiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai J","key":"weweralbrechtsenpau","last":"Wewer Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philipp E","key":"geyerpau","last":"Geyer","locid":"fc987200-bf00-477b-8c57-e83a7984b89e","name":"Geyer, Philipp E.","name_org":"Geyer, Philipp E","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Sophia","key":"dollpau","last":"Doll","locid":"b65237bb-c5a2-41d7-87ca-d6be89cb4b26","name":"Doll, Sophia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter V","key":"treitpau","last":"Treit","name":"Treit, Peter V","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirstine N","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","locid":"0c7b0831-8bcd-4ed4-84d6-565f8424f3e9","name":"Bojsen-Moller, Kirstine N.","name_org":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christoffer","key":"martinussenpau","last":"Martinussen","name":"Martinussen, Christoffer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nils B","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nils B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Signe S","key":"torekovpau","last":"Torekov","locid":"c1d71a61-ee09-4c29-ae48-7520707a73be","name":"Torekov, Signe Sørensen","name_org":"Torekov, Signe S","orcid":"0000-0001-6779-0252","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Florian","key":"meierpau","last":"Meier","name":"Meier, Florian","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lili","key":"niupau","last":"Niu","locid":"f74df5eb-9404-4bdb-9d58-289bf2c90efa","name":"Niu, Lili","orcid":"0000-0003-4571-4368","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alberto","key":"santospau","last":"Santos","locid":"75866a6a-0c79-4882-b550-a6c550000e21","name":"Santos, Alberto","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Eva C","key":"keilhauerpau","last":"Keilhauer","name":"Keilhauer, Eva C","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Matthias","key":"mannpau","last":"Mann","locid":"f463f571-68c5-44fb-bff1-bb9d748fcda8","name":"Mann, Matthias","orcid":"0000-0003-1292-4799","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30528273"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cels.2018.10.012","issn":["24054712"],"issue":"6","journal":"Cell Systems","pages":"601-612","status":"p","title":"Cell Systems","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85059240341"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6445e470-eef1-4503-81f8-510861746fbb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Plasma Proteome Profiling Reveals Dynamics of Inflammatory and Lipid Homeostasis Markers after Roux-En-Y Gastric Bypass Surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453382","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The heart is a central human organ and its diseases are the leading cause of death worldwide, but an in-depth knowledge of the identity and quantity of its constituent proteins is still lacking. Here, we determine the healthy human heart proteome by measuring 16 anatomical regions and three major cardiac cell types by high-resolution mass spectrometry-based proteomics. From low microgram sample amounts, we quantify over 10,700 proteins in this high dynamic range tissue. We combine copy numbers per cell with protein organellar assignments to build a model of the heart proteome at the subcellular level. Analysis of cardiac fibroblasts identifies cellular receptors as potential cell surface markers. Application of our heart map to atrial fibrillation reveals individually distinct mitochondrial dysfunctions. The heart map is available at maxqb.biochem.mpg.de as a resource for future analyses of normal heart function and disease.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Doll, Sophia","Dreßen, Martina","Geyer, Philipp E","Itzhak, Daniel N","Braun, Christian","Doppler, Stefanie A","Meier, Florian","Deutsch, Marcus-Andre","Lahm, Harald","Lange, Rüdiger","Krane, Markus","Mann, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-415430"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"region and cell type resolved quantitative proteomic map of the human heart","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-017-01747-2","version":"Published Versio